ll},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-07-23T21:45:39Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T13:39:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nIt is surely there for 4.3-4.5 versions of Godot\n\n### System information\n\n-\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e0603aeda3ce0e15c5843f5202172a56f3ff5534/core/io/packet_peer_udp.cpp#L312\n\nUpon receiving a data via _poll or udp server's poll, PacketPeerUDP copies it into its local variable recv_buffer, after that another copying into ring buffer occurs.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e0603aeda3ce0e15c5843f5202172a56f3ff5534/core/io/packet_peer_udp.cpp#L125\n\nWhen the data is read by get_packet, another copying to packet_buffer occurs. get_packet's behavior is somewhat understandable: user may not use the received pointer until the next call of get_packet. However, in my opinion, there at least should be some interface to read data directly from ring buffer. On the other side, poll's copying is totally unnecessary and has to be removed. As a result 3 times less data would be copied.\n\nMoreover ring buffer copies data with for loop. memcpy should be used instead, as for loop may not be optimized with some compilers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n-\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108918/reactions","total_count":0,